  <h2>Who I am</h2>
  <p>
    I'm a software and platform engineer based in Eindhoven. I work where cloud
    infrastructure meets software that has to be provably correct — most
    recently as a Technical Consultant at Philips Image Processing &amp;
    Solutions, through Enter B.V.
  </p>

  <h2>What I do</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Cloud and security.</strong> I designed and deployed the first AWS WAF
    on a Philips platform, delivered as infrastructure-as-code: OWASP Top 10 rules,
    IP filtering, DDoS mitigation, and automated rule updates, with CloudWatch logging
    and alerting behind it.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Delivery in a regulated environment.</strong> I refactored the Health
    Analytics Engine and wrote the PDLM/QMS-compliant design documentation to go with
    it. I set up the BDD environment used in its verification and validation process
    and introduced it to the V&amp;V team. I led the migration of a legacy field-study
    system to a modern platform and tightened its CI/CD pipelines for stable releases.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Automation and agentic AI.</strong> I build with Claude, MCP servers,
    GitHub Copilot and n8n — and I've driven adoption of those workflows among senior
    colleagues, not just used them myself. I write MCP servers, not just prompts.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Systems that have to keep working offline.</strong> During my Philips
    internship I extended BATDOK with IPFS-backed peer-to-peer sharing so medical
    records stay available in low-connectivity field environments, via an Android
    plugin bridging Kotlin and Go.
  </p>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>
    I care about the boring parts: documentation that survives an audit,
    pipelines that don't need babysitting, and infrastructure someone else can
    pick up without me. Most of my work has been in environments where "it works
    on my machine" isn't an acceptable answer.
  </p>

  <h2>Beyond the stack</h2>
  <p>
    I'm bilingual English/Mandarin and have spent four years as a part-time
    solution architect for a Chinese trading business — building out its WeCom
    platform and integrating digital tools with day-to-day operations. If your
    company works across the EU and China, I've done that translation in both
    directions. I studied ICT Software Engineering &amp; Cybersecurity at Fontys
    and served as President of Proxy, its ICT study association, where I built
    the Microsoft 365 and Entra ID environment from scratch and managed a €150k+
    budget.
  </p>
